    "q-4346": {
      "dom_id": "step-q4346",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182820/assets/8eeeb4e409d681d34dcc4c4926e9da8c1759b96e6a28517d5ee2837d4d98f4ed.png)\n\nIf the side that is opposite to a ${45}^{∘}$ angle in an isosceles right triangle has a length of $4,$ what is the length of the hypotenuse?",
      "worked_solution": "The hypotenuse in an isosceles right triangle is equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg.\n\nThe legs of an isosceles right triangle are the sides that are opposite the ${45}^{∘}$ angles. So in the given triangle, the legs have length $4.$\n\nConsequently, the hypotenuse has a length of\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 4=4\\sqrt{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
