      "source_example_id": "e-3080",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Length of the Legs of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given the Hypotenuse",
      "kp_id": "e-3080"
    },
    "q-22025": {
      "dom_id": "step-q22025",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182820/assets/1073020fe8576784ed24601864f8546a72b426d8f02670b1a8c13923dc16e35f.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the triangle above is $16+8\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of the hypotenuse.",
      "worked_solution": "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=16+8\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 16+8\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 16+8\\sqrt{2} & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 8(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =a(2+\\sqrt{2}) \\\\ 8\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =a\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} \\\\ 8 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length of each leg is $a=8,$ and the length of the hypotenuse is\n\n$$\nAC=a\\sqrt{2}=8\\sqrt{2}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
