      "source_example_id": "e-3085",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Length of a Hypotenuse or Leg of a 45-45-90 Triangle Given its Perimeter",
      "kp_id": "e-3085"
    },
    "q-119321": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119321",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14182820/assets/70d961102240b0c48132baca8db0b77ed80ff8e0d3b7296bd5c727ab2f97dfd3.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $18+9\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg.",
      "worked_solution": "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=18+9\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 18+9\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 9(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 9(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 9\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 9 & =a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $9.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
